From: Waltteri Hooli <wahooli@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] local: soc: qcom: icc-bwmon: release the DDR bandwidth vote across system sleep

icc-bwmon watches LLCC<->DDR traffic and, from its threaded IRQ, votes a DDR/LLCC
bandwidth OPP with dev_pm_opp_set_opp(). The vote is ACTIVE_ONLY and the only
thing that ever lowers it is another IRQ. The driver has no dev_pm_ops, so across
a system sleep the IRQ is quiesced and whatever bandwidth it last voted stays
applied for the entire suspend.

On this platform (Lenovo Yoga Slim 7x, X1E-80-100) that is the s2idle floor.
s2idle here never reaches the RPMh sleep set -- aosd/cxsd/ddr stay at 0, the APSS
only collapses in short episodes ended by the ADSP tick and never takes the DDR
self-refresh vote -- so the DDR frequency during "sleep" is governed by the
standing ACTIVE votes, and bwmon's is the largest dynamic one. Suspend from idle
and bwmon has already ramped to its minimum: s2idle draws 590 mW. Suspend right
after a workload and bwmon is pinned high, frozen there for the whole suspend
because its IRQ cannot fire:

  idle           -> s2idle 590 mW
  after mpv       -> s2idle 862 mW
  after cpu load  -> s2idle 1130 mW    (15 min suspends, same boot, no hibernate)

The residue is not hibernate related -- it reproduces on a cleanly booted kernel
-- and it survives the full 15 min because nothing services the down-migration.

Give bwmon a system-sleep suspend/resume pair: stop the monitor and release the
OPP vote (dev_pm_opp_set_opp(dev, NULL)) at suspend so DDR falls to the aggregate
of the other, already quiesced, consumers; re-arm the monitor at resume, where
the first IRQ re-applies a real vote. SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS covers s2idle and every
hibernation phase.
---
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/icc-bwmon.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/icc-bwmon.c
@@ -815,6 +815,40 @@
 	free_irq(bwmon->irq, bwmon);
 }
 
+static int bwmon_suspend(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct icc_bwmon *bwmon = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+	/*
+	 * Nothing services the bwmon IRQ across a system sleep, so the bandwidth
+	 * it last voted stays applied for the whole suspend. On this platform
+	 * s2idle never reaches the RPMh sleep set (the DDR self-refresh vote is
+	 * never taken), so that stale ACTIVE vote governs the DDR frequency the
+	 * entire time the machine is "asleep": suspend right after a workload and
+	 * DDR is pinned at its busy corner until resume, for hundreds of mW.
+	 *
+	 * Stop the monitor and release the vote so DDR falls to the aggregate of
+	 * the other, already quiesced, consumers. bwmon_resume() re-arms the
+	 * monitor and the first post-resume IRQ re-applies a real vote.
+	 */
+	bwmon_disable(bwmon);
+	dev_pm_opp_set_opp(bwmon->dev, NULL);
+	bwmon->current_kbps = 0;
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static int bwmon_resume(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct icc_bwmon *bwmon = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+	bwmon_start(bwmon);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static DEFINE_SIMPLE_DEV_PM_OPS(bwmon_pm_ops, bwmon_suspend, bwmon_resume);
+
 static const struct icc_bwmon_data msm8998_bwmon_data = {
 	.sample_ms = 4,
 	.count_unit_kb = 1024,
@@ -879,6 +913,7 @@
 	.driver = {
 		.name = "qcom-bwmon",
 		.of_match_table = bwmon_of_match,
+		.pm = pm_sleep_ptr(&bwmon_pm_ops),
 	},
 };
 module_platform_driver(bwmon_driver);
